//
// Expected: a0 at one session, a1 at two. Knowing k does not supply the
// secret associated data ad. The attacker cannot construct a different
// ciphertext accepted by Bob. The companion with leaked ad permits a concrete
// forgery. Declared nonces keep the ciphertext identical across sessions,
// and that is what fails at two: the attacker leaves Alice unstarted and
// replays Alice#2's n_c and c to Bob, so Bob and Bob#2 both decrypt a
// ciphertext Alice sent once. Bob generates s only after accepting c, so
// nothing he contributes binds it. Every session once had to start, so both
// Alices sent c. The forgery question is answered at one session.

attacker[active]

principal Alice[
	knows private k
	knows private ad
	leaks k
	knows private plain
	knows private n_c
	c = AEAD_ENC(k, n_c, plain, ad)
]

Alice -> Bob: n_c, c

principal Bob[
	knows private k
	knows private ad
	m = AEAD_DEC(k, n_c, c, ad)?
	generates s
	out = HASH(s, m)
]

Bob -> Alice: out

queries[
	authentication? Alice -> Bob: c
]
